OL,3,GNEWSADrinks giant Diageo apologises
OL,4,Aafter Moray burn pollution
OL,5,
OL,6,FDrinks giant Diageo has apologised
OL,7,Fafter a pollution incident in Moray
OL,8,Fwhich killed a significant amount of
OL,9,Fwildlife earlier this year.
OL,11,FA chemical, thought to be caustic soda,
OL,12,Fis understood to have entered the water
OL,13,Fat the Knockando burn at some time in
OL,14,Flate April or early May. At the time
OL,15,Ffly fishers said its salmon population
OL,16,Fhad been wiped out and could take years
OL,17,Fto recover.
OL,19,FDiageo has apologised for the damage
OL,20,Fcaused to the local environment, and
OL,21,Fthe impact on river users and the wider
OL,22,Fcommunity.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
